.TH DF 1
.SH NAME
df \- disk space
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B df
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B df
is a command built into the shell,
.BR sh (1).
It prints the disk's label, its size and free space in KiB, the space that
becomes free after the next commits (blocks a commit still keeps for
safety), and the number of objects (files, directories, links).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR stat (1),
.BR snap (1),
.BR siefs (5)
